    {
      "id": "2262613a397697fada420cf1a945a97f9e99f026",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2610082260,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> Please, can somebody tell my how to change the commit message with git.\n\nFrom the command line, `git commit -a --amend` lets you make code changes *and* commit-message changes to a commit.\n\nThe problem there is that \"Add support to call ssl_starttls_ack() and ssl_starttls_post_ack() from dissectors written in LUA\" is 96 characters long.\n\nI think that long lines *after* the first line tend to be line-wrapped for you, but the first line, which Git operationally and culturally treats as a summary of the commit, isn't wrapped.  Maybe \"Add support to call STARTTLS helpers from Lua\", for example, would work.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-07-07T22:10:07.921Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-07-07T22:10:07.921Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 396936825,
